  "summary_en": "Bahrain's iGA Cloud First Policy (v1.0, April 2017) requires government entities to consider cloud services first in all ICT procurement. It sets out migration criteria, security principles, data classification and data sovereignty rules, and assigns roles to iGA, ICTGC and SCICT. It does not cover AI or robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "All government agencies must evaluate cloud-based services in all ICT procurements",
   "Adopts the NIST definition of cloud computing and its deployment and service models",
   "Covers cloud security principles, data classification, backup and data sovereignty",
   "iGA acts as the interface with cloud service providers and manages SLAs",
   "ICTGC oversees implementation and audits entities for compliance"
  ],
